   <row>
    <id><![CDATA[2186609]]></id>
    <qid><![CDATA[2283590]]></qid>
    <question><![CDATA[<h1>Informed Consent of Participation</h1>

<p>You are invited to participate in the online study <strong>"User Study on Workflow Documentation"</strong>, conducted as part of a bachelor's thesis under the supervision of the principal investigator.</p>

<p>Before participating, please note:</p>

<ul data-spread="false">
	<li>Participation is voluntary.</li>
	<li>You may discontinue your participation at any time before submitting your responses.</li>
	<li>The study takes approximately 20–40 minutes.</li>
	<li>Basic demographic information (e.g., age and gender) will be collected.</li>
	<li>Participation is anonymous and no personally identifying information will be collected.</li>
	<li>Repeated participation is permitted.</li>
</ul>

<p>Please read the following information carefully before deciding whether to participate.</p>

<h3>1. Purpose of the Study</h3>

<p>The purpose of this study is to compare two approaches for automatically generating workflow documentation from a user perspective.</p>

<p>Participants will <strong>read</strong> workflow documentation generated by each approach and answer questions about its content. The goal is to investigate whether a self-developed agentic documentation approach provides advantages over a GPT-based documentation approach regarding understanding, perceived usefulness, confidence, and user preference.</p>

<h3>2. Procedure</h3>

<p>After providing consent, you will:</p>

<ol data-spread="false" start="1">
	<li>Complete a short questionnaire about your background and experience.</li>
	<li>Review a workflow documentation and answer comprehension questions.</li>
	<li>Evaluate the documentation using usability and confidence questions.</li>
	<li>Repeat the procedure with a second workflow documentation.</li>
	<li>Indicate your preferred documentation and provide final feedback.</li>
</ol>

<h3>3. Risks and Benefits</h3>

<p>No significant risks are associated with participation in this study. Participation is not expected to provide any direct personal benefit, but your contribution will support research on automated documentation generation.</p>

<h3>4. Data Protection and Confidentiality</h3>

<p>All responses will be treated confidentially and analyzed anonymously.</p>

<p>The collected data will be used exclusively for research purposes as part of a bachelor's thesis and related academic publications or presentations. No information that could identify individual participants will be published.</p>

<p>All data will be handled in accordance with applicable data protection regulations, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>

<h3>5. Contact Information</h3>

<p>If you have any questions regarding this study, please contact:</p>

<p>Laura Pfeil<br />Student Researcher<br />laura.pfeil@student.hu-berlin.de</p>

<p>Prof. Dr. Thomas Kosch<br />Principal Investigator<br />Rudower Chaussee 25<br />12489 Berlin, Germany<br />thomas.kosch@hu-berlin.de</p>

<h3>6. Informed Consent and Agreement</h3>

<p>This consent form will be retained securely and in compliance with the GDPR for no longer than necessary.</p>
]]></question>
