</result_path></result_path></result_path></result_path></result_path></result_path></code></pre>

<p>These files support reproducibility by preserving the exact configuration and annotation inputs used for a run.</p>

<h2 id="65-temporarily-disabled-igv-report">6.5 Temporarily disabled IGV report</h2>

<p>An IGV report target exists in the Snakefile but is commented out:</p>

<p>igv_report = os.path.join(result_path, "igv-report.html"),</p>

<p>So IGV report generation appears to be planned or previously supported, but it is not currently part of the active target set.</p>

<h1 id="7-resources-and-logging">7. Resources and Logging</h1>

<p>rule all sets:</p>

<ul>
	<li>memory from config["mem"], defaulting to 4000</li>
	<li>threads from config["threads"], defaulting to 1</li>
	<li>log file at logs/rules/all.log</li>
</ul>

<p>Implication</p>

<p>These resource declarations apply to the aggregate rule and do not necessarily reflect the needs of the individual underlying rules. Actual heavy compute behavior is likely defined in the included rule files.</p>

