<hr />
<h1 id="workflow-description">Workflow Description</h1>

<h2 id="key-workflow-steps">Key Workflow Steps</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p>Loads project configuration, sample annotations, and a gene list, then derives visualization groups from both bulk-style group labels and single-cell metadata files.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>Builds a genome-track workflow setup for a defined set of genes or genomic regions, including validation and normalization of requested gene targets.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>Records genes that cannot be resolved from the provided genome annotation and prepares a cleaned gene annotation table for downstream processing.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>Incorporates shared, environment export, preparation, and visualization rule modules to generate genome track outputs and browser-compatible resources.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>Produces final outputs including genome track files, a UCSC track hub configuration, exported environment files, and copies of key configuration and annotation tables in the results directory.</p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="workflow-overview">Workflow Overview</h2>

<p>This workflow supports the generation of genome track visualizations for a defined set of genes or genomic regions, together with browser-ready outputs and archived workflow configuration. It is useful in projects that need consistent, reproducible inspection of signal patterns across genomic loci from annotated BAM-based samples, including both standard grouped samples and single-cell datasets with metadata-defined subgrouping. By combining sample annotations, a user-provided gene/region list, and genome-based coordinate resolution, the workflow organizes per-locus track outputs, prepares a UCSC track hub, and records unresolved gene entries. It is relevant for researchers who need shareable genome-browser views and project-specific track figures for comparative analysis across sample groups.</p>

<h1 id="rule-overview">Rule Overview</h1>

<h2 id="rule-overview-1">Rule Overview</h2>

<hr />
<h2 class="unnumbered" id="rule-all">Rule: all</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Final target rule collecting the required genome track files, track hub file, exported environment files, and configuration/annotation outputs.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><strong>Input</strong>:</p>

	<pre>
<code>expand(os.path.join(result_path, 'tracks', '\{gene}.'+config["file_type"]), gene=genes)
os.path.join(result_path, "bigWigs", config["genome"], "trackDb.txt")
expand(os.path.join(result_path,'envs','\{env}.yaml'),env=['pygenometracks','igv_reports','sinto'])
os.path.join(result_path,'configs','gene_list.csv')
os.path.join(result_path,'configs','\{}_config.yaml'.format(config["project_name"]))
os.path.join(result_path,'configs','\{}_annot.csv'.format(config["project_name"]))</code></pre>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><strong>Output</strong>:</p>

	<pre>
<code>-</code></pre>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><strong>Dependencies</strong>: None identified on visible rules.</p>
	</li>
</ul>

<hr />
<h2 class="unnumbered" id="external-rules">External Rules</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p><code>common.smk</code></p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>envs_export.smk</code></p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>prepare.smk</code></p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>visualization.smk</code></p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h1 id="configuration-and-environment">Configuration and Environment</h1>

<h2 id="configuration-file">Configuration file</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p><code>config/config.yaml</code></p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="configuration-loading">Configuration loading</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p>Loaded via <code>config/config.yaml</code>.</p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="accessed-configuration-parameters">Accessed configuration parameters</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p><code>sample_annotation</code>: path to the sample annotation table loaded with <code>pandas.read_csv</code>.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>gene_list</code>: path to the gene list table loaded with <code>pandas.read_csv</code>; used to define genomic regions/genes and associated <code>ymax</code> values.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>result_path</code>: base output directory; combined with the module name <code>genome_tracks</code> to define workflow result locations.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>file_type</code>: output file extension for generated genome track files in the main target rule.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>genome</code>: genome identifier used in the UCSC track hub output path.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>project_name</code>: used to name exported configuration and annotation files.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>mem</code>: memory resource for rule <code>all</code>, accessed via configuration file with default <code>4000</code>.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p><code>threads</code>: thread count for rule <code>all</code>, accessed via configuration file with default <code>1</code>.</p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="explicitly-defined-versions">Explicitly defined versions</h2>

<ul>
	<li>
	<p>Snakemake minimum version: <code>8.20.1</code></p>
	</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="further-reading">Further Reading</h2>

<p>For details on Snakemake configuration and workflow setup, see the official Snakemake documentation: https://snakemake.readthedocs.io/en/stable/snakefiles/configuration.html</p>
]]></question>
